# Gate out - the leaving track chopped away on eighths.
#
# A gate is a square wave on the fader, and writing one by hand was thirty-two keyframes
# nobody could read. `every` writes it in a line, which is the only reason this file is
# short enough to be worth having.
#
# Eighths rather than sixteenths on purpose. The whole score is stepped at the redraw
# rate - fifty milliseconds while a beat-aligned transition runs - so an eighth of a bar
# at 128 BPM is about five steps of the loop and reads as a gate, where a sixteenth is
# two and reads as a stutter with a limp. That is the ceiling of what a *lane* can chop;
# past it the move belongs to `loop`, which is playback and not a control.

name    Gate out
note    the leaving track chopped away on eighths
bars    4
align   beat
tempo   match
power   free

lane out gain
    bar 0    1.0    hold
    every 1/8 from bar 1 to bar 3   1.0 0.0   hold
    bar 3    0.0    hold
    bar 4    0.0    hold

# Opening from a whisper underneath the gate, so the holes in it are filled by the new
# track rather than by silence.
lane in gain
    bar 0    0.0    smooth
    bar 3    1.0    hold
    bar 4    1.0    hold

lane in highpass
    bar 0    400    smooth
    bar 3      0    hold
    bar 4      0    hold

lane in tempo
    bar 0    0.0    hold
    bar 3    0.0    smooth
    bar 4    1.0    hold

hook bar 1    toast ░ gate
